  "root_causes": [
    "The old overnight solver maximised distance and distinctness across the global candidate catalogue, so a Sauerland selection could be routed through Belgium/Luxembourg/eastern Germany.",
    "The selected destination had only a small score bonus and was not a hard route anchor.",
    "Plan-time overnight discovery could collide with the background discovery lock and then fall back to the legacy generic destination discovery path.",
    "Anchor-specific discovery queries were ordered after origin-wide queries, so the early candidate stop could finish before the chosen region was searched.",
    "The roadtrip live-candidate profile still estimated motorcycle travel at a legacy 72 km/h.",
    "The generic accommodation provider treated motorcycle + 'any' as non-camping and did not score motorcycle access, secure parking, garage or covered parking."
  ],
  "fixes": [
    "Canonical pure overnight solver anchors short roadtrips to the selected destination region and rejects unrelated routes.",
    "Five-day trips require four distinct overnight regions with >=50 km road movement.",
    "Destination-anchor discovery now runs before broad origin discovery and is explicitly invoked when the selected plan lacks overnight supply.",
    "Plan supply no longer calls legacy discoverLiveOptions as a fallback.",
    "Motorcycle planning uses 55 km/h with a 350 km comfortable-day cap.",
    "A single final vehicle-aware accommodation authority discards the generic accommodation result; motorcycle 'any' accepts camping and lodging and ranks motorcycle access/parking/garage/covered parking."
  ],
